      'Pick how many frames to save and press Save frames. Every image is full size and upright; download them one by one or in a single zip.',
      'The video stays on your device the whole time.',
      'One thing PNG cannot do is undo the compression the video already had when it was recorded. Blockiness or blur in the MP4 is still there in the PNG. What PNG avoids is a second round of lossy compression on top, and that matters when you are going to edit the still: cutting out a subject, upscaling it, adjusting colours or placing text over it all make JPG compression marks more visible, while a PNG frame gives each of those steps the cleanest starting point the video allows.',
      'PNG is also the better choice for screen recordings. Text, code and interface elements have hard edges that JPG blurs into a faint halo, while a PNG frame of a screen capture stays crisp and is often smaller than you would expect, because large flat areas of colour compress well without loss. From camera footage the reverse is true: a PNG of a busy 1080p scene is often several times the size of the same frame as a JPG, for a difference you will rarely see.',
